. Their responsibilities encompass both technical procedures and patient education, ensuring comprehensive care for individuals under their supervision.\",9\r\n914,CÓDIGO DE DIETAS,\"CÓDIGO DE DIETAS is a comprehensive document that records all available diets in a hospital, specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of patients. It serves as a systematic framework that categorizes these diets, ensuring proper dietary planning and management. The Diet Code outlines the standards and guidelines necessary for effective dietary management within the hospital setting, facilitating the provision of appropriate nutrition to patients.\",6\r\n8231,MÉDICOS,Médicos are doctors who assess patients' nutritional status and collaborate with the Unidad de Nutrición for dietary needs.,5\r\n15922,PACIENTES SANITARIOS,Patients who are receiving healthcare services and may be affected by nutritional issues.,3\r\n14867,CATÉTER CENTRAL,\"Central catheters are used for temporary access in patients requiring infusion for more than 15 days, with specific complications associated with their use.\",7\r\n8400,DIETA PARA NEUTROPENIA,\"A specialized diet for patients undergoing chemotherapy or bone marrow transplants, aimed at reducing the risk of infection by avoiding high-risk foods.\",1\r\n8238,PERSONAL DE COCINA,Kitchen staff responsible for food preparation and ensuring hygiene standards are met in hospital kitchens.,1\r\n1601,PREMIO BEST IN CLASS,\"The Premio Best in Class is an award recognizing the best nutrition unit, which has been awarded to the Sección de Nutrición at Hospital La Fe.\",1\r\n8233,REGLAMENTO 1169/2011,\"A regulation in the European Union that sets legal standards for food information to consumers, including nutritional labeling in collective dining settings like hospitals.\",1\r\n8232,RESOLUCIÓN RES AP (2003) 3,\"A resolution by the Council of Europe regarding food and nutritional care in hospitals, establishing recommendations for improving patient care.\",1\r\n